{"text": "From: Tobias Lindqvist <tlindqvist@lindqvistmarsh.example>\nTo: \"Castellanos-Webb, Renata\" <rcw@cwstern-law.example>\nCc: Nadia Haddad <nhaddad@lindqvistmarsh.example>\nDate: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:42:07 -0700\nSubject: Okafor Family Trust v. Meridian Coastal Title - No. 24-CV-018832 - meet and confer re RFP Set Two\n\nRenata,\n\nFollowing up on our call Tuesday. I am writing under Code Civ. Proc. § 2031.310 before we\nfile anything, and I'd much rather not file anything.\n\nYour client's responses to the Trust's second set of document requests, served September 18, 2026,\nare deficient in three respects:\n\n1. RFP No. 14 (wire authorization records). Meridian Coastal Title & Escrow Co. produced the\noutgoing wire confirmation for the $487,250.00 disbursement on June 3, 2025 but not the\nauthorization log. We know from Seabright Community Bank's subpoena response that the wire went to\nan account ending in 7617 at a bank in Ireland (IBAN IE08 AIBK 3848 4972 3876 17) that\nhas nothing to do with my client. Somebody at Meridian approved the changed instructions. We are\nentitled to know who and from where.\n\n2. RFP No. 17 (login records). The escrow platform logs you produced (Bates MCT-000412 through\nMCT-000498) stop on May 30. The changed wire instructions were uploaded June 2. Please produce the\nlogs for June 1-4, 2025, including source IPs. For what it's worth, Seabright's records show\nthe confirming email was opened from 203.0.113.47 and again from 2001:db8:4c2::1f, neither of\nwhich is a Meridian office as far as we can tell. Your escrow officer Gordon Pruitt testified he\nwas \"working from home that week\"; Mr. Pruitt's home connection should be easy to rule in or out.\n\n3. Privilege log. There isn't one. Forty-one documents were withheld.\n\nOn your side: you asked for the trustee's deposition. Ifeoma Okafor is available November 10 or\n12, at our office. Please note Ms. Okafor observes Friday prayers and cannot do the 13th.\nShe will need breaks; she is recovering from chemotherapy and I will hold you to\nseven hours over two days if needed.\n\nIf I don't have supplemental responses and a log by October 29, 2026, I will file the motion\nwith a separate statement under Rule 3.1345 and ask for $2,850 in sanctions, which is what\nthis has cost the Trust so far. I have also uploaded our own supplemental production to\nhttps://share.lindqvistmarsh.example/s/okafor-meridian-prod04 (password by separate email).\n\nCall me. I'm in tomorrow until 3.\n\nTobias\n\nTobias Lindqvist | Lindqvist Marsh LLP\nState Bar No. 284471\n1900 Soquel Avenue, Suite 410, Santa Cruz, CA 95062\nDirect (831) 555-0172 ext. 214 | Fax 831-555-0109\n\nThis message may contain privileged information. If you received it in error, delete it\nand let me know.\n\n> On Oct 13, 2026, at 9:05 AM, Renata Castellanos-Webb wrote:\n> Toby - can we talk at 2? Castellanos-Webb & Stern, P.C. is closed Monday so I am buried.\n> I'll have Pruitt's calendar by then. - RCW", "kind": "Email", "detail": "476 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Tobias Lindqvist", "Renata Castellanos-Webb", "Nadia Haddad", "Okafor Family Trust", "Ifeoma Okafor", "Gordon Pruitt", "Tobias", "Pruitt"], "companies": ["Lindqvist Marsh", "Meridian Coastal Title", "Seabright Community Bank", "Lindqvist Marsh LLP", "Castellanos-Webb & Stern, P.C."]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.30000000074505806, "modelMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 6, "end": 22, "text": "Tobias Lindqvist", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Tobias Lindqvist"}, {"start": 24, "end": 57, "text": "tlindqvist@lindqvistmarsh.example", "kind": "email", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "tlindqvist@lindqvistmarsh.ex